WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:09.790
Hillary Clinton and Donald Trump. Donald
Trump and Hillary Clinton. Hillary Trump

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:13.960
and Donald Clinton. No matter how you
rearrange their names something is really

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.160
really wrong with our political system
right now. You know this to be true

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.240
whether you're a political junkie or if
you couldn't name the vice president if

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.890
your life depended on it.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.180
Our broken system churning out
uninspiring candidates, coupled with our

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.340
broken media that often just repeats
campaign talking points, has given us two

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.930
broken candidates from two broken
parties competing in a broken election

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.690
for control of a nation going broke.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.410
This isn't how it was supposed to be nor
is it how it has to be.

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:49.539
I don't particularly like Hillary
Clinton or Donald Trump. Hillary has been

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:53.860
involved in the political machine for
the past 30 years at various levels from

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.879
wife of a governor, to first lady, to
Senator, to Secretary of State and it's

00:00:57.879 --> 00:01:01.359
not really clear to me if her
accomplishments outweigh her poor

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:02.289
decisions.

00:01:02.289 --> 00:01:07.090
Nothing she says strikes me as real or
honest, like how she's constantly railing

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.590
against wall street while at the same time
taking at least 25 million dollars from

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:16.689
Wall Street this campaign cycle alone. At
a time when we're all frustrated by the

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:22.750
system she is the ultimate insider
trying to maintain her grip on power. Add

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:28.299
her willful ineptitude at best, or gross
negligence at worst with her emails,

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:33.310
her questionable decisions in Iraq and
Libya and the Clinton Foundation's ties

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:38.799
to various foreign governments, and there
is a lot of questions about her campaign.

00:01:38.799 --> 00:01:42.430
She also constantly plays into the
social justice and oppression Olympics

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:47.979
which judges us all as groups rather
than individuals, and a pretty sure you

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:49.840
guys know how I feel about that.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:56.500
As for Trump even after all these months
of campaigning I still have no real idea

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:02.469
what he thinks about any issue. He seems
to have a staggeringly low amount of

00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:06.490
knowledge about basic policies or how
the government is designed to work.

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:12.040
Do you really think he knows the different
duties of the executive legislative and

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.620
judicial branches of government? The fact
that I can't say so for sure that he

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:22.660
does is extremely concerning to say least. I
also don't sense he has any sort of

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:27.640
moral Center other than what's good for
him at the very moment. He will say

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.930
anything, quite literally anything, to
stay in the news and we simply have no

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:37.240
idea how he would govern. His comments
constantly tow the line between fact

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.130
and fiction, and he seems deeply
uninterested in other opinions than his

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:45.640
own. While many think he'll shatter the
monster of political correctness

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.380
currently assaulting us it seems like a
tall order for someone who threatens

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.580
to ban news organizations and sue
reporters when they ask him hard

00:02:54.580 --> 00:03:00.250
questions, or challenge his statements. So how did we possibly get to a place where

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.410
everyone I talk to is either
begrudgingly voting for one of these two

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.630
people or just won't vote at all?

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:13.150
How did we end up with too deeply
unpopular polarizing people who

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:18.160
seemingly represent the worst of us as
the only two legitimate candidates for

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.260
the highest office in the land?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.580
It's probably time we looked in the
mirror and saw our own responsibility in

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.769
this unfolding clown show. The writing
has been on the wall for years. We watch

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:34.060
garbage reality shows, some of them
hosted by future presidential candidates,

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:40.330
we read biased listicles full of gifs
instead of actual news articles. We say

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.739
vicious things to people online that we
would never say to their faces. Our

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:48.820
thoughts have been reduced to six second
videos, one hundred hundred and forty character

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:54.610
sentences, filtered images, and mindless
snaps. We reward the Kardashians with

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.640
fame and fortune while we can't come up
with the money to take care of our

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.380
veterans. We watch news channels that are
nothing but mouthpieces for the

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.780
political parties. We shame, and slander
and de-platform people we disagree with.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:13.930
We issue trigger warnings and safe spaces
instead of promoting true education and

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.109
open discussion. We ask for better
leaders but then we don't vote

00:04:18.109 --> 00:04:23.419
on election day. We complain but we don't
get involved. When you step back and you

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:27.560
think about all of this it's pretty
obvious why we got left with these two

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:33.020
candidates. Now allow me to make the
quick case of why you should vote for

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:37.340
each one of these people in case you
didn't think I was going to do that. With

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.750
Hillary, you know what you're going to
get. Our system is messed up but she's

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.620
part of it and she's damn well going to
make sure that the wheels don't come off

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.479
during her watch.

00:04:47.479 --> 00:04:51.529
She's a known quantity in that she cares
about her legacy and she doesn't want to

00:04:51.529 --> 00:04:56.569
see the country crumble after spending
her entire life trying to get to this

00:04:56.569 --> 00:05:00.800
very place. In short if you think things
are going ok

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.449
it makes sense to vote for Hillary. The
case for Trump is totally the reverse.

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:10.099
He's an unknown quantity andn the system
hates him. He's giving a voice to middle

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:14.240
America that is usually ignored or
mocked by the elite. He represents the

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.800
greatest threat to this social justice
fiasco infecting all levels of society.

00:05:19.849 --> 00:05:25.099
he's used the political system and our
pathetic media against itself. In short,

00:05:25.099 --> 00:05:28.490
if you think that things are really
messed up and we have to change it at

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.810
any cost

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:34.729
then it absolutely makes sense to vote
for Trump. I for one, despite everything

00:05:34.729 --> 00:05:38.960
I've said here, think that the truth lies
somewhere in between. There is no

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.520
question that our system is screwed up
but the truth is, it's still one of the

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:48.110
best ones out there and despite our
flaws. Americans have freedoms which make

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:53.300
people all over the world envious. People
still look to America as a beacon of

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.889
light in the world. People still want to
move here, and most of us don't want to

00:05:57.889 --> 00:05:58.819
move out.

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:04.310
We have an imperfect system but a system
that can and will survive these two

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:08.509
imperfect candidates. Some people are
voting for Hillary because they think

00:06:08.509 --> 00:06:13.520
she's the last line of defense against
Trump who they liken to Hitler. Some

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.449
people are voting for Trump because they
think he's the only way to stop Hillary

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:19.639
the Manchurian candidate.

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:22.529
What a sad and pathetic state were in.

00:06:22.529 --> 00:06:27.359
Hillary, a candidate saying she can fix
everything that's wrong even though it's

00:06:27.359 --> 00:06:31.589
her team who's been in power for the
past eight years, and Trump a man who's

00:06:31.589 --> 00:06:36.389
staggering lack of worldly knowledge
outside of his own tiny bubble is

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:40.979
somehow considered an asset by his
supporters. Now before I tell you who I'm

00:06:40.979 --> 00:06:43.949
going to support and why, I want to say
one more thing.

00:06:43.949 --> 00:06:48.389
Whoever you choose in this election, I'm
actually okay with it.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:51.569
Probably the most important thing I've
been fighting for with this show is the

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:56.249
ability to agree to disagree. To sit
across from someone and hear their ideas

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.289
and make your own judgment call.

00:06:58.289 --> 00:07:02.549
I don't ask that you agree with my
guests or even myself in this case. I

00:07:02.549 --> 00:07:07.829
don't ask that you support who I support,
nor agree with my reasons for supporting

00:07:07.829 --> 00:07:13.439
them. What I hope for, not ask for, is that
all of us whether you support Hillary or

00:07:13.439 --> 00:07:19.679
Trump, are able to sit across from people
who support the other person. That

00:07:19.679 --> 00:07:24.839
regardless of who someone votes for we
realize we have two candidates but one

00:07:24.839 --> 00:07:29.849
country, and most importantly that people
are able to make different choices than

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:34.199
you for different reasons, and that
doesn't mean they're mean or evil or

00:07:34.199 --> 00:07:39.449
even worse - gross and racist. I spent a
lot of time on The Rubin Report talking

00:07:39.449 --> 00:07:41.159
about the role of government.

00:07:41.159 --> 00:07:45.539
it's something so important, yet in our
public discourse we rarely talk about it,

00:07:45.539 --> 00:07:49.709
even as government gets bigger and
bigger. Both the Democrat and Republican

00:07:49.709 --> 00:07:55.079
conventions were perfect examples of
this. At the DNC, speaker after speaker

00:07:55.079 --> 00:07:58.199
talked about how Hillary could solve all
of your problems.

00:07:59.129 --> 00:08:02.309
I guess she's had all the answers this
whole time but just forgot to tell them

00:08:02.309 --> 00:08:06.869
to her old pal Barack. Every speaker,
including Hillary herself, said that she

00:08:06.869 --> 00:08:11.489
has the answers and that government
under her watch can solve everything.

00:08:12.239 --> 00:08:17.579
The RNC wasn't very different though, for
a series of other reasons. Trump and his

00:08:17.579 --> 00:08:21.449
speakers talked about how corrupt the
system is but their answer was that

00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:24.119
Trump, and Trump alone could fix it.

00:08:24.119 --> 00:08:28.889
Immigration? Well only Trump has the
answers. The economy? Only Trump could fix

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:29.680
it. Terrorism?

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:34.390
Only Trump could keep us safe. In
both cases the answer to everything was

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:39.490
bigger government. Your decisions, be
economic or personal, should be given to

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.409
you by the government.

00:08:41.409 --> 00:08:45.190
This concept has been creeping on us for
a long time, and now we have two

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:50.200
candidates that think they are the only
ones who know how to live your life, even

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.220
better than you do.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.779
There is simply only one way out of this
mess, and I don't think it involves

00:08:55.779 --> 00:09:00.610
propping up a broken system or burning
it down altogether. Every election we

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:04.630
hear this is the most important election
in a generation, but you know at this

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:09.550
time it actually might be true. Despite
everything, we deserve better than this

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:13.899
endless battle between Republicans and
Democrats who are more concerned about

00:09:13.899 --> 00:09:17.680
their grip on power than they are
addressing the needs of the people that

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:22.180
they're supposed to serve. There is only
one way to take the power away from

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:28.270
their monopoly over our lives. We must
from this election forward put both the

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:33.070
Democrats and the Republicans on notice
that they no longer have a stranglehold

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:39.670
on the political process in America. The
only way we can do this is to starve

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:44.680
them. We must starve them of our
attention, of our money, and our votes.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.410
Their diet must begin right now.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:51.610
For these reasons and some others I'll
be supporting Libertarian candidate Gary

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.950
Johnson for President the United States.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.790
I don't think Gary is the perfect man
nor the perfect candidate, and I suspect that

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.240
he doesn't think he is either - but he's
sure better than these other two options.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:05.680
As a libertarian, Gary doesn't want to
tell you who you can marry and what you

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:11.500
can smoke. He wants lower taxes and to
empower local, not federal government,

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.400
which in my view is always a good thing.
He wants to give the power back to the

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:19.480
people to control their own lives. He
wants a fair resolution to our

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:24.130
immigration problem, and he acknowledges that radical Islam - especially in the

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:29.050
form of Sharia law, is a real threat. He
wants a strong military so that we won't

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:34.180
have to use it, not so that we can go on
military adventures and nation build. His

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:38.460
blend of being fiscally conservative and
socially liberal is really

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:42.330
where I think most people are
ideologically but we just never get the

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:46.380
chance to choose it. I do have some
differences with Gary, and the

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:50.610
Libertarian Party in and of itself is a
total mess, but i think he best

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.910
represents the ideals I would want in a
president.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:57.660
Sometimes you have to stand on principle
even when you know the result will be a

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:02.100
short-term loss. Now before you guys tell
me I'm throwing my vote away let me lay

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:05.970
out a plan here. I think that if you've
listened this far you acknowledge that we

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.710
do have a problem here.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:11.640
Well the only way we're ever going to
solve this problem is by getting more

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:17.280
voices heard, not less. If Gary gets to
fifteen percent in an average of national

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:22.080
polls then they have to put him in the
Presidential Debates. Why not have at

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:28.440
least one debate with another voice. At the
absolute bare minimum we deserve to hear

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:33.510
one different point of view now more
than ever. I don't need a president to be

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:37.890
my savior, but maybe having an
alternative to the two-party strangle hold

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:43.560
on American politics is actually what
can save us. The polling maybe antiquated

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:47.730
and many only use landlines instead of
cell phones, but I think if there was

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:52.530
enough public support to get Gary to
fifteen percent they would have to put

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.190
him in.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:57.810
I don't think Gary's even a particularly
good debater but how about once, just

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:03.510
once, for the first time since Ross Perot in
1992 we get a third person on that

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:07.980
debate stage. From now until the debates
Gary Johnson has my support. While I

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:11.550
acknowledge that he will not be
president, nor do I agree with him on

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:16.230
everything I think he best represents
the ideals that I want to see from our

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:21.360
government and our president. If we're
ever going to fix this broken mess we

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:26.640
must start now. Let's show the Democrats
and the Republicans that they don't own

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:32.310
us, but they do owe us. They owe us the
chance to hear more voices because they

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:37.080
damn well haven't done a great job while
they've been in charge. If Gary doesn't

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:40.590
hit the fifteen percent threshold or
does one debate and then his support

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.120
falters I'll decide what to do at that
time.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:48.670
Regardless, I think that the classical
liberal and libertarian ideals that Gary

00:12:48.670 --> 00:12:52.870
embodies more than either of the other
two candidates can truly, and should

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:58.210
truly, be the future of American politics.
We need a new generation of leaders who

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:03.640
believe in these ideas to wake up right
now but it just isn't going to happen by

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:09.339
itself. So let's put the people in power
on notice and let them know that we

00:13:09.339 --> 00:13:13.779
won't be sleeping until 2020. Instead
we're going to make sure that they know

00:13:13.779 --> 00:13:19.210
with absolute certainty that this is
their last free ride before the rest of

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.650
us are heard.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:25.660
Alright, so there you go. Simply by the
math alone I suspect that my choice with

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:29.830
have more people angry at me then either of the other two choices could have, but I

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:33.400
hope that whether you agree with me or
whether you disagree with me, that you

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.110
respect the rationale in the logic that
I've used to come to my decision. At the

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:41.470
end of the day one of these people will
be President and we're still all going

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:45.940
to be here so let's try to be better
than them, before Canada builds a wall, to

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.110
keep us all out.

